From 4a4b7ac87e7ab96d2accb886115bc82e11c4c94e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 18:46:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(v1.2): Team/RBAC, S3-compatible storage, reliable
 file-by-file generation engine
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Prisma schema: Organization/Team/OrganizationMember/TeamMember, StageAssignment,
  RevisionRequest, ArtifactObject, ReminderLog. All additive — existing 3 models
  (User/Project/ArtifactStage) extended with nullable FKs, no breaking changes.
- RBAC: RolesGuard + Roles decorator, org-level enforcement; stage-level assignment
  permission enforced in StagesService.decide() (needs stageKey context).
- Teams + Members modules (FR-601-606). MailService is a log-only STUB — this repo
  has zero SMTP integration, flagged explicitly.
- AuthService: auto-provisions an Organization+OWNER membership for the existing
  single-admin account and for new Google sign-ups, so V1.2 doesn't require manual
  setup on top of the existing single-admin flow. /auth/me now returns organizationId.
- Stages: 3-way decision (approved/rejected/revision_requested), stage assignment,
  stage + project deadlines, revision history endpoint.
- Storage module: S3-compatible client (MinIO by default). Folder structure is
  users/{userId}/projects/{projectId}/artifacts/... per bug report — NOT
  organizations/.../stages/... Added because this repo had NO object storage at
  all before this (content was stored as plain text in Postgres).
- Generation/Validation engine: sandboxed Docker validators for backend (tsc),
  frontend (tsc+build), database (ephemeral Postgres + migration), self-healing
  counter (max 3, tracked on ArtifactStage). New webhook endpoints upload-file and
  validate-stage for n8n's file-by-file generation loop to call.
- docker-compose.yml: added MinIO service + docker socket mount on backend
  (sandbox validation needs to spawn containers).

NOT included in this patch: n8n workflow changes (file-by-file generation prompts,
3-way Check Approval switches) — those are separate n8n-side changes, not backend
code. Reference patterns already validated and deployed as standalone n8n workflows
in a prior session; applying them to this repo's actual production workflow needs
explicit confirmation before touching a live n8n instance.

Prisma migration NOT generated/run in this patch — sandbox has no network access
to binaries.prisma.sh (blocked) and no DATABASE_URL to a real Postgres. Run
'npx prisma migrate dev --name v1_2_governance' after applying.
